        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12543849/comment/13220994",
          "id": "13220994",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Good work Mete!\n\nThere is still something I believe the patch did not address yet: RepositoryStatisticsImpl implements Iterable.\nThis contract implies that if I call #iterator() I'll get back all the existing entries.\nI would expect that if I define a custom entry, it should still be returned in the #iterator() call, otherwise some consumers of the api will not be able to see all the existing TimeSeries.\n\nAnother minor issue is a method in the RepositoryStatisticsImpl: private Type getType(String type)\nI think this would be better located in the Type enum, as RepositoryStatisticsImpl doesn't really need to deal with identifying a Type by its name.\n\nI find it interesting that there are no unit tests in the patch. One test case could very well be the #iterator() problem described earlier.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2012-03-02T15:33:10.145+0000",
          "updated": "2012-03-02T15:33:10.145+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12543849/comment/13221007",
          "id": "13221007",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=meteatamel",
            "name": "meteatamel",
            "key": "meteatamel",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436"
            },
            "displayName": "Mete Atamel",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Thanks for the feedback. Regarding getType method, yes, definitely, it makes more sense as a static method on Type enum. Regarding the iterator though, I'm not sure how to solve that, that's why I kind of left it the way it is. The problem is that the returned iterator has the following signature: \"Entry<Type, TimeSeries>\". As you know, with the changes, now we can have String as type and I cannot return those String based types from this iterator. I can change the iterator's signature to \"Entry<String, TimeSeries>\" and that would enable me to return all the entries but then I'd be changing a public method. So, I'm not sure which one is worse: return some of the values from the iterator or change a public method.  ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=meteatamel",
            "name": "meteatamel",
            "key": "meteatamel",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=meteatamel&avatarId=13436"
            },
            "displayName": "Mete Atamel",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2012-03-02T15:56:11.031+0000",
          "updated": "2012-03-02T15:56:11.031+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12543849/comment/13221031",
          "id": "13221031",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
